# =============================================================================
# Atlas Sanctum — .gitignore
#
# Open-Core Philosophy
# ====================
# .gitignore is NOT a tool for protecting intellectual property.
# It only prevents local or generated files from being committed to Git.
#
# Proprietary source code belongs in SEPARATE PRIVATE REPOSITORIES:
#
#   Public (this repo)          Private (separate repos)
#   ──────────────────          ────────────────────────
#   atlas-protocol              atlas-intelligence
#   atlas-sdk                   atlas-market-engine
#   atlas-cli                   atlas-governance-ai
#   atlas-docs                  atlas-finance-engine
#   atlas-examples              atlas-enterprise
#   atlas-plugins               atlas-cloud
#
# What belongs here:
#   Secrets, credentials, API keys, generated files, build artifacts,
#   local caches, OS/editor noise, and runtime data.
#
# What does NOT belong here:
#   AI models, proprietary algorithms, enterprise business logic,
#   internal datasets, premium features, commercial APIs.
#   → Those go in private repos, accessed via stable interfaces.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# SECRETS & CREDENTIALS — Never commit. Ever.
# =============================================================================

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Deep nested catch-all — no .env anywhere in the tree
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example

# Key files
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
!*.key.example
!*.pem.example

# Secret stores
